{actorOne.name} waves something in your face, to heat up your emotions into a sizzling pâté of excited investment. A pad sweeps into view, showing a woman [[living life to her absolute coolest->Theosebeia_Video]].

:: Theosebeia_Chill
actorTwoOver: true
actorOneViewing: "Required viewing,"
actorOneViewing (actorOne.personality === "stooge" || actorOne.personality === "hothead"): "Look. Look! LOOK,"
actorOneViewing (actorOne.personality === "nerd"): "You'll want to etch this into your brain holes,"
--

{actorTwo.name} pops around the corner. "What are you two talking about?"

{actorOne.name} whips out a pad, waving it in {actorTwo.name}'s face. {capitalize: actorOne.pronouns.subject} notices you outside of {actorOne.pronouns.dependent} field of vision, and motions you to come closer, to join {actorTwo.name} in an impromptu semi-circle to bear witness. "{actorOneViewing}" {actorTwo.pronouns.subject} says, shaking the pad with vigor. You catch a [[small figure towards the edge of the screen->Theosebeia_Video]].

:: Theosebeia_Video
Debris clouds the screen, rocks sliding into frame to obscure the woman sitting on her grav board. Just as quickly, they pass by; she is one of two constants in this field of rock and metal. A broken planet rests in the bottom of the frame, a hole straight through the center pointing back out towards an enormity of stars. The scoreboard is at about a minute and a half left, and counting. Announcers are excitedly sharing details as she hoists herself into an upright standing position. If she can't make a winning play now, she's out, they breathlessly chatter. Theosebeia has been giving upsets this whole game, but a few chokes midway through leaves no room for error. She's got time for one big score, and that's it.

In a flash, so fast you barely notice it, she's diving. Her board accelerates down, engines burning through what remains of the ozone below as the camera tilts to follow. Color commentators are screaming, desperate to understand the world in a moment as Theosebeia rockets towards the planet's core. You try to understand the words pouring out of the mouths of the folks in the sound booths. Surely, pulling 5 Gs down is a huge boon, but will that be enough? Will she wipe out before making the points she needs? A risky gamble, they deride. Theosebeia has been the underdog this whole time, but there's no reason to think that she'll be able to-

She can hear them. A psychic force letting her know how to upset, how to drive these folks wild. There are 30 seconds left on the clock, and Theosebeia is at maximum speed, accelerating as much as her board can handle; according to your overlay she's at about 20 Gs. She's rocketing through, going faster and faster, straight towards the center of the planet. You find yourself holding your breath. Even knowing this is a recording, you feel like any utterance of sound would break history. Would end an otherwise astonishing moment.

The screaming announcers become wailing sirens. Theosebeia has left her board, gliding without control or stability into the heart of a moon. The only consolation she has is that the hole is at least a few miles in diameter; enough for you to see, enough for any mistake to be fatal. Her board is rocketing around the equator towards the other side, presumably on some automatic control. Theosebeia and the moon are practically touching, 20 seconds left as the camel disappears inside the eye of the needle.

They've cut to a second camera, the other side of this ruined, dead crust. There's no one to document what must be an incredible moment as she strides through rock, heat, the bones of a planet devoid of life and opportunity. Stripped for resources, fracked for every last drop. This will be its history, this will be the defining moment of not only this world, but an entire generation. You notice her board rocket into frame, right at the other side of the hole. You think you can parse the groans and hampered breaths of the commentators; Theosebeia has *got* to touch her board, or she earns no points. History is *happening* in this moment. You are now a part of the legend that will be etched into eons after today, even in this facsimile of a recording.

Nine seconds left on the clock. Nothing. Eight. Your eyes are watering, glued to the hole, to catch any sign, any hope of what is about to happen. Seven. You forgot what it means to breathe. You can remember, later. Maybe. Six. Your heart is pounding in your chest. Five.

It is at this precise moment that Theosebeia comes screaming out of the mouth of hell. A pinprick in a gaping maw, she expands to recognizable size in the photon sensors of the camera. Four. Her board accelerates a little ahead of her, trying to match her velocity to make what happens next a little easier. Three. Her hand is outstretched, reaching for the board. Two. You can't tell if they're a mile or a meter apart. There is no sense of depth but the stars, the terrible awful blackness blanketed in tiny little thimbles of light. One. The board is slowing down, trying to let her catch up, as if reaching out in desperation. Fingers straining to mesh together, fighting to connect. Zero.

Her hand is on the board. "HER HAND IS ON THE BOARD!" The announcers, once silent are now screaming everything you've been too afraid to say. Unbelievable. Let no one forget Theosebeia and this legendary maneuver. "AS THE TEN ARBICQUARES OF ORION ARE WITNESS, LET IT BE KNOWN THAT THEOSEBEIA IS THE WINNER; THE NOW TWO-TIME GRAV BOARDING CHAMPION OF THE AQUAMARINE CUP!" They're panting, straining to let out each sentence as they struggle to regain any sense of reality. Millions of fans are screaming in the distance, silenced only as {actorOne.name} dims the pad and pulls it away.

<!-- TODO: Notes on how the sport is a little less dangerous than it appears to be. Their suits detect collisions and will deploy measures to slow down players. So in fact, the hole Theosebeia just punched through is even narrower than it appears (otherwise her suit would have begun to save her life)-->